<title>USA: Stiglitz sees US solid growth, moderate inflation.</title>
<headline>Stiglitz sees US solid growth, moderate inflation.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House economic adviser Joseph Stiglitz said Friday he believes the U.S. economy will enjoy solid economic growth with moderate inflation in 1997.</p>
<p>Stiglitz issued the statement after the Labor Department reported the U.S. economy created 262,000 new jobs last month, with the unemployment rate holding steady at 5.3 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Today's report confirms that our economy is continuing to run at solid and sustainable levels,&quot; Stiglitz said. &quot;We believe that the economy will continue into 1997 on a healthy and balanced course with moderate inflation and solid economic growth.&quot;</p>
</text>
